4697	Service installed
4720	User account created
4728 / 4732	Added to privileged groups
4740	Account locked out
4768 / 4769	Kerberos authentication
4776	NTLM authentication
1102	Audit log cleared

These are especially important for banking security monitoring.

Dashboards

In Wazuh / OpenSearch create dashboards for:

* Failed logons by branch
* USB device insertions
* Wi-Fi adapter installations
* Privileged group changes
* New local administrator accounts
* PowerShell execution
* RDP logons
* Branch PC compliance status

Alerting

Configure alerts for:

* More than 10 failed logons in 5 minutes
* USB storage insertion
* Wi-Fi dongle installation attempt
* Audit log cleared (1102)
* Local admin group modified
* New service installed
* BitLocker disabled
* Windows Defender disabled

Alerts can be sent by email, Microsoft Teams, Slack, Telegram, or SMS gateway.

Recommended for Rupali Bank

Since you already use Wazuh, I would deploy:

* 2 Domain Controllers
* 1 Dedicated WEF Server (Windows Server 2022)
* 1 Wazuh Server (Rocky Linux 9, 16 vCPU, 64 GB RAM, 2 TB SSD)
* Wazuh Agent on every branch PC and server
* Sysmon deployed through GPO
* 90-day online retention
* Daily backup of OpenSearch indices